# Binary files the leak gate cannot scan, reviewed by eye and recorded here.
#
# The gate refuses binaries by default because grep -I skips them, so it would
# otherwise report CLEAN on a file it never read -- which is exactly how a
# coverage database carrying absolute home-directory paths reached a public repo.
#
# Adding a path here is a statement that a human looked at the file. For a UI
# screenshot that means checking for a hostname or address in a URL bar, a
# connection panel, a tooltip or a breadcrumb.
#

# (no reviewed binaries in this repository yet)
